---
description: Release, packaging and GitHub publication rules
globs: "VERSION,BUILD_CHANNEL,docs/CHANGELOG.md,README*.md,docs/releases/RELEASE_*.md,scripts/**,.github/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

- `packaging/VERSION`, `APP_VERSION`, README artifact names and release notes must agree.
- `BUILD_CHANNEL=INTERN` intentionally blocks public release publication.
- Run `./scripts/check_release.sh` before release packaging/publication.
- Preserve reproducible ZIP/source/DEB/RPM/developer-package and SHA256 generation.
- After every successful version build, follow `docs/project/RELEASE_BACKUP_POLICY.md`: archive the complete result outside the repository and retain and verify the newest two versions.
- Require a clean committed worktree and explicit project-owner approval before GitHub publication.
- `BUILD_CHANNEL=INTERN` still permits a normal, explicitly requested push to a non-release development branch and an explicitly requested pull request; this is not public release publication.
- Tags, public releases, force-pushes and remote deletion are separately authorized actions. Never treat permission for one action as permission for another.
- Do not create a public release from an internal build merely because tests pass.
